d performance  benchmarks of the M2 Pro and M2 Max  chips with pretty poor performance  compared to expectations just look at  how Intel's chips destroy the M2 Max and  both single core and multi-core this  points to the M2 Pro and mass shifts  being based on the same five nanometer  again which would be the worst case  scenario because they were already  delayed until this spring of 2023 so we  all assumed they'd be built on three  nanometer because of that delay but what  if Apple both delayed and kept the chips  on the same process node or maybe even  giving it the four nanometer process  which is essentially just refined five  nanometer in terms of technology and it  also doesn't help that tsmc greatly  increased the prices and even forced  Apple to pay those higher prices for  their silicon nodes because of all of  the supply chain and inflationary issues  so it seems like all of these supply  chain issues are causing Apple to give  us underwhelming products especially on  the Apple silicon side and it's all due  to these supply chain issues that  bloomed from the pandemic and got  exponentially worse because of Apple's  hardcore Reliance on Taiwan and China  and now on the other hand from Apple's  perspective it could make sense to give  us underwhelming products like the M2  iPad Pro which essentially only got a  chip swap and not much else the reason  for that is that Apple probably knows  that a deep recession is here and it  doesn't make sense to put your best  products out there during a time when  people aren't willing to pay more for  the best products it probably just makes  sense to give us the same old thing  again just refined a bit more just for  Apple to continue their sales and  marketing throughout the recessionary  period until they can get a more Clear  Vision of how the next couple of years  will pan out but keep in mind that when  they eventually do end up giving us  these killer products when things settle  down the prices will also likely 